                     (trunk/src/LV2/faust-generated/gx_flanger.cc and stereoverb.cc,
                      trunk/src/LV2/DSP/gx_pluginlv2.h)

Changed files. Everything is unchanged except three files whose oversampling
used zita-resampler (which needs threads MSVC lacks) and a variable-length
array (which MSVC doesn't accept): GxEternity/dsp/eternity.cc,
GxSuppaToneBender/dsp/vstb_clip.cc and GxSuperFuzz/dsp/sfp_clip.cc. Each says
so at the top and marks every change "Ikaros:". The resampling is taken out
and Ikaros oversamples those stages itself (juce::dsp::Oversampling, see
GxPedalPlugin in src/engine/PortedPedals.h).

Also not used: the SuppaToneBender and SuperFuzz wrappers' step that runs
the DSP at 48 kHz when the session runs at 96 kHz or more (a CPU saving).
Here they run at the session's rate.

To add a pedal: copy its dsp/ folder and LICENSE here, add a file like
ikaros/GxSD1.cpp and a namespace in ikaros/GxDsp.h, and list the file in
ikaros/CMakeLists.txt.
